{"id":"maintenance_guide#e1","hash":"81b0514780370c0a","type":"noise","subtype":"header","parent":null,"page":0,"characters":43,"md":"Solar Schools Programme - Maintenance Guide"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e2","hash":"1387a1b2dd552ee2","type":"heading","level":1,"parent":null,"page":0,"characters":44,"md":"# Solar Schools Programme: Maintenance Guide"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e3","hash":"1d6e55e2159d170e","type":"paragraph","parent":"maintenance_guide#e2","page":0,"characters":118,"md":"This guide tells school staff how to keep a rooftop solar installation working. **Read it before the first cleaning.**"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e4","hash":"c38a8563992a0648","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"maintenance_guide#e2","page":0,"characters":19,"md":"## 1. Monthly tasks"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e5","hash":"0965354c6e39b4e3","type":"paragraph","parent":"maintenance_guide#e4","page":0,"characters":42,"md":"Do these tasks once a month, on a dry day:"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e6","hash":"f909e28dbb3730fd","type":"list","parent":"maintenance_guide#e4","page":0,"characters":134,"md":"- Clean every panel with water and a soft cloth\n- Check that no cable is loose or exposed\n- Write the inverter reading in the log book"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e7","hash":"6a757a1a063476a9","type":"heading","level":3,"parent":"maintenance_guide#e4","page":0,"characters":22,"md":"### 1.1 Cleaning steps"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e8","hash":"7436a5cb5e9f67cd","type":"list","parent":"maintenance_guide#e7","page":0,"characters":116,"md":"1. Switch off the inverter\n2. Rinse the panels from the top down\n3. Switch the inverter on and check the green light"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e9","hash":"e5e4f0869f32d0eb","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"maintenance_guide#e2","page":0,"characters":19,"md":"## 2. Who does what"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e10","hash":"6fbb24a3cdcce293","type":"caption","parent":"maintenance_guide#e9","page":0,"characters":25,"reference":"maintenance_guide#e11","md":"Table 1: Responsibilities"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e11","hash":"93e6a710df6df4fd","type":"table","parent":"maintenance_guide#e9","page":0,"characters":175,"md":"| Task | Person | How often |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Cleaning | Caretaker | Monthly |\n| Inverter check | District engineer | Quarterly |\n| Log review | Head teacher | Monthly |"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e12","hash":"8398543d1ca1a253","type":"paragraph","parent":"maintenance_guide#e9","page":0,"characters":77,"md":"The next table shows the fault codes; the first column is shared by two rows."}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e13","hash":"bc8d788f4ecdd6fc","type":"table","parent":"maintenance_guide#e9","page":0,"characters":128,"html":"<table>\n<tr><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Action</th></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\">E1</td><td>Low voltage</td><td>Wait for sunlight</td></tr>\n<tr><td>No voltage</td><td>Call the engineer</td></tr>\n</table>","md":"| Code | Meaning | Action |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| E1 | Low voltage | Wait for sunlight |\n| E1 | No voltage | Call the engineer |"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e14","hash":"20b2f9058bb6577e","type":"caption","parent":"maintenance_guide#e9","page":0,"characters":20,"reference":"maintenance_guide#e13","md":"Table 2: Fault codes"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e15","hash":"ab85f693817f2bc7","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"maintenance_guide#e2","page":1,"characters":26,"md":"## 3. A clean installation"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e16","hash":"93e41cbc803b5a76","type":"image","parent":"maintenance_guide#e15","page":1,"characters":31,"file":"images/maintenance_guide_e16.png","md":"Figure 1: Panels after cleaning"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e17","hash":"956571f033806418","type":"caption","parent":"maintenance_guide#e15","page":1,"characters":31,"reference":"maintenance_guide#e16","md":"Figure 1: Panels after cleaning"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e18","hash":"f0d8fe972b933720","type":"paragraph","parent":"maintenance_guide#e15","page":1,"characters":81,"md":"Panels should look like this after every cleaning. *Dust cuts output by a fifth.*"}
{"id":"maintenance_guide#e19","hash":"4627b70ad7fe4e04","type":"quote","parent":"maintenance_guide#e15","page":1,"characters":35,"md":"> A clean panel is a working panel."}
